# Build context for backend/Dockerfile and backend/Dockerfile.cpu is the
# repository root (see docker-compose.yml), because alembic.ini lives at the root
# and the entrypoint runs `alembic upgrade head`.
#
# Deliberately a deny list rather than `*` plus negations. An allowlist that
# starts with `*` has to re-include every path the build needs, and getting that
# wrong fails as a missing file deep inside a multi-minute image build. A deny
# list fails loudly and early if something needed is excluded, and keeps the two
# things the build actually copies -- alembic.ini and backend/ -- included by
# default.
#
# Everything below is excluded because it is either not read by the runtime, or
# must never ship: secrets, caches, other services' dependency trees, local
# databases and model weights.

# --- version control and CI ---------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# --- other services -----------------------------------------------------------
# The frontend has its own image and its own context (./frontend), so none of it
# belongs in the backend build. node_modules alone is hundreds of MB.
frontend/

# A .dockerignore is read from the *context root*, and BuildKit prefers
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over it. frontend/.dockerignore therefore governs
# the frontend build (context ./frontend) and this file governs the backend build
# (context .). The frontend/node_modules pattern below is not redundant with
# `frontend/` above: it is what keeps the host dependency tree out of the context
# if the frontend build is ever moved to the repository root, which is where it
# would have to move to share a layer cache with the backend.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/

# --- local state that must not be baked into an image -------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/
logs/
results/
models/
saved_models/

# --- model weights ------------------------------------------------------------
# No foundation encoder ships (see the REMOVED register in
# backend/tests/test_reachability.py and docs/deployment.md §3). A stray
# multi-GB checkpoint in the working tree must not become an image layer.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.bin

# --- caches and build artefacts -----------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- test-only artefacts ------------------------------------------------------
# backend/tests/ itself is kept: it is a few hundred KB, and pruning by directory
# here risks more than it saves. Test *output* is excluded above.
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Documents (docs/, README, CHANGELOG) are left in the context on purpose. They
# cost a few hundred kilobytes, and a `*.md` deny pattern is the kind of rule
# that silently excludes something a later change turns out to need. The things
# worth excluding are the ones measured in gigabytes: .git, frontend/, weights,
# local data directories and caches.
